<br/> <br/>Hoping to return someday... sigh.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by pgirish007: where is this place? may be I should move there so that next time when you walk around you can take my photograph along with the location :D   Burano is part of the City of Venice. It''s an island about 45 minutes northeast of the main island by Vaporetto (water bus). Murano, another island much closer to Venice is well-known for it''s beautiful glass. Burano is known as a fishing village and for its handmade linen and lace. The entire island is full of brilliant multicolored buildings. Many of the residents pay careful attention to complementary colors and stage the outside of their homes with coordinated accessories, tools, etc. For photographers, skipping Murano and taking the time to get to Burano a great option. Hoping to return someday... sigh.', '2020-09-16 13:31:20.000000', NULL, 0),
